-- title:
--   Uniform node presentation over one inertia-fixed number field
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$, a positive level $N$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$; let `data` be a modular polynomial datum for $q$ (a monic $\Phi$ of degree $\psi(q)$ in the $j$-expansions) satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \equiv (C(X)^q-X)(C(X)-X^q) \bmod q$, let $h\alpha,h\beta$ assert integrality of the two degeneracy maps from level $N$ to level $Nq$ on Laurent base change, let $P$ be a place specialisation of level $N$ at $A$ with reduction $\mathrm{red}$, and let $R$ be a prolongation tuple over $P$ (two regular prolongations $R_1,R_2$ of $A$ to the level-$Nq$ function field over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$, compatible with the Atkin–Lehner involution and with the reductions). Assume $q\nmid N$, that $\mathrm{red}\,c=0$ exactly for $c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$, that $R$ is a model (the two divisor laws and the two cusp laws) and satisfies the fixed-place order law, and that for a finite set $W$ of places $w$ of the geometric level-$N$ function field over $k$, each of them supersingular (rational, affine in $j,j_N$, with supersingular $j$-value), $R$ satisfies the regularity law and the node-value law for $W$. Then there is a number field $K_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbf Q}$ such that: every element of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbf Q$ fixes $K_0$ pointwise; an element $d$ of $A\cap K_0$ reduces to $0$ under $\mathrm{red}$ if and only if $d\in q\,(A\cap K_0)$; and there is a family of node coordinates $(x_w,y_w)$ over $K_0$, one for each $w\in W$, in the node ring $\mathcal O_w(K_0)$ of functions integral for $R_1$, for $R_2$ and at all places of level $Nq$ above $w$ and with coefficients in the field generated by $K_0$, such that for all $w\in W$: $x_w y_w = q^{\,e_q(w)}u_w$ with $u_w$ a unit and $e_q(w)$ the characteristic-$q$ width $\mathrm{jWidthChar}$ of the $j$-value of $w$ divided by the ramification index of $j$ at $w$; the ideal $(q,x_w,y_w)$ is maximal and is the only maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_w(K_0)$; $(q,x_w)$ and $(q,y_w)$ are prime with $y_w\notin(q,x_w)$ and $x_w\notin(q,y_w)$; $\mathcal O_w(K_0)$ is noetherian; and for every $g\in\mathcal O_w(K_0)$ there is $o\in A\cap K_0$ with $g-o$ a non-unit.
--
--   This is the local presentation of the special fibre of $X_0(Nq)$ at the supersingular points in the Deligne–Rapoport picture, made uniform in the node: one inertia-fixed number field of definition serves all places of $W$ simultaneously, and at each of them the node ring is a local noetherian ring with two branches crossing with intersection multiplicity the characteristic-$q$ width. It feeds the good-class criterion [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.isGoodClass_of_extendsToPlace_pts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.isGoodClass_of_extendsToPlace_pts).
